# Managed by the website repo (ops/caddy/form-limits.caddy, #124). ops/caddy-limits.sh copies
# it to /etc/caddy and imports it into each site block that serves the app. Change it in the
# repo, not on the server.
#
# Caps the request body on the public form endpoints, so an oversized POST is cut off at Caddy
# (413) after 256 KB instead of being read in full by Node. That covers the REST endpoint and
# GraphQL, where form submissions can also be created. The app's own limit on a submission is
# about 20,000 characters (src/modules/contact/domain/submissionSize.ts), at most about 80 KB of
# JSON even in a script that takes several bytes per character, so 256KB never blocks a real
# message.
#
# The agents' MCP endpoint (#336) shares the cap: one MCP request carries one tool call (a find,
# or one suggested event or post), a few KB of JSON, so 256KB never blocks a real one. Payload
# reads the whole body before the plugin sees it.
#
# The OAuth token address (#1501) shares it too: a token request is a few short form fields, and
# the app cuts a body off at 8 KB itself as it arrives, so Caddy's cap only keeps the rest of an
# oversized one from reaching Node at all.
@sprecherEastFormSubmissions path /api/form-submissions /api/form-submissions/* /api/graphql /api/graphql/* /api/mcp /oauth/token
request_body @sprecherEastFormSubmissions {
	max_size 256KB
}
